target: mf repo restore
summary: Put a backup of a repository back (the most recent one by default)

!! Reference

```
Put a backup of a repository back (the most recent one by default)

The backup is checked first; the current store is set aside under .metafolder/internal/pre-restore-*. Everything written since the backup is lost: run `mf reconcile` afterwards to catch up with the files. The repository is the selected one, or — when its store no longer loads — one named by --path/--metafolder; either way it is loaded afterwards.

Usage: mf repo restore [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --from <FROM>
          The backup directory (default: the most recent one under .metafolder/internal/backups/)

      --path <PATH>
          The repository's root, instead of a selected repository

      --metafolder <METAFOLDER>
          The repository's external .metafolder directory, instead of a selected repository

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
```
